// SOT land patterns (library plan W4, item 3c wave 1).
//
// Frame convention: CoHDL's board frame (+x right, +y DOWN, top view),
// origin at the package centre. SOT-23-3 lands are authored on the frame of
// transistor::FP_JSCJ_SOT23 0.2.0, which the assembler measured on the
// 2026-10-30 preview board: the datasheet top view (pins 1 and 2 on the
// lower edge, pin 3 on the upper edge) turned 90 degrees so that pins 1 and 2
// form the +x column, pin 1 at +y (lower right), pin 2 at -y and pin 3 alone
// at -x. Numbering stays counter-clockwise 1-2-3 seen from the top; the
// mirrored arrangement (pin 1 at -y) would swap pins 1 and 2 on the board.
//
// Names follow RFC-021's checked template SOT{pins}P{pitch}X{bodyX}X{bodyY}N.
// The checker reads the pitch as the closest distance between distinct pad
// numbers, which on SOT-23-3 is pins 1-2 at 1.90mm (not the 0.95mm lead
// pitch), so the name reads P190 (E809).

// SOT-23-3 (TO-236AB). Primary source: Zhuhai Hongjiacheng MMBT5551
// datasheet Rev 2.0, page 3, "Suggested Pad Layout" (evidence record
// docs/hongjiacheng-mmbt5551.evidence.md): J (land width along the row)
// 0.75-0.85mm, K (land length across the row) 0.85-0.95mm, M (row centre
// spacing) 1.95-2.05mm, N (pin 1 to pin 2 centre spacing) 1.85-1.95mm. The
// land uses the midpoints: 0.80 x 0.90mm lands, 1.90mm pin 1-2 spacing and
// 2.00mm row spacing.
//
// Cross-check: Diodes Incorporated SOT23 package information, Rev.
// 2017-01-30, page 1 (docs/diodes-sot23.evidence.md): X = 0.8mm, Y = 0.9mm,
// C = 2.0mm, X1 = 1.35mm (centre line to the outer edge of pin 2, i.e.
// 0.95mm + 0.40mm), Y1 = 2.9mm. Identical to the primary midpoints.
// transistor::FP_JSCJ_SOT23 (JSCJ S8050, 0.6 x 0.8mm lands, 2.02mm rows) is
// compared in docs/README.md.
//
// The pad is declared in the datasheet's top-view orientation (0.80mm along
// the row, 0.90mm across it) and placed `rotate 270`, as FP_JSCJ_SOT23 does.
pub pad P_SOT3P190X290X130N_LEAD {
    shape: rect
    size: (0.8mm, 0.9mm)
    layer: top_copper
    plating: smd
}

// Name digits from the primary page-3 outline: D (body length) 2.80-3.00mm,
// nominal 2.90; E (body width) 1.20-1.40mm, nominal 1.30.
#[doc("docs/README.md")]
pub footprint SOT3P190X290X130N {
    pad 1: P_SOT3P190X290X130N_LEAD at (1mm, 0.95mm) rotate 270
    pad 2: P_SOT3P190X290X130N_LEAD at (1mm, -0.95mm) rotate 270
    pad 3: P_SOT3P190X290X130N_LEAD at (-1mm, 0mm) rotate 270
    silkscreen {
        pin_1_marker near pad 1 shape dot
    }
    // Contains the 2.90 x 2.70mm copper and the 2.55 x 3.00mm maximum
    // component envelope (E1 lead span x D body length) with at least 0.25mm
    // excess on every side.
    courtyard { shape: rect, at: (0mm, 0mm), size: (3.4mm, 3.6mm) }
    silkscreen_ref { at: (0mm, -2.5mm) }
}
